## Issue / Resolution

### BE-E1-001: Perfect-fifth direction naming

- Observation: A progression such as `V -> I` has a pitch-class interval of 5 when calculated from the first degree to the target degree, while the reverse subtraction used by secondary-dominant detection is 7.
- Resolution: `isPerfectFifthDown(from, to)` uses the semantic progression direction and checks interval 5. Existing secondary-dominant logic retains its reverse subtraction because it asks whether the changed dominant is seven semitones above the target.
- Test: Both shared interval helpers and existing secondary-dominant regression behavior pass.

